---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About NO BALL GAMES | Sign-Flip Culture and the Grime Art Backbone"
  description="About NO BALL GAMES, the restricted-space sign flip, and Charlie Buster's Grime Art layer presented with clear lore-versus-proof guardrails."
  current="about"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1>From warning sign to cultural system.</h1>
    <p>
      NO BALL GAMES starts with a British restriction sign and turns it into a brand built on art, rebellion, collector culture and story. The message is simple: denied space can still become owned space.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">The sign flip</span>
      <h2>Restriction became identity.</h2>
      <p>
        The phrase "No Ball Games" was built to control public play in estates, courts and shared urban spaces. This brand flips that instruction into a street-culture symbol: create anyway, play anyway, leave a mark anyway.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is the foundation for the site, projects, collections and lore.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Truth labels</span>
      <h2>How claims are handled.</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li><strong>Verified:</strong> backed by accessible source material.</li>
        <li><strong>Internal canon:</strong> accepted brand/lore truth inside this universe.</li>
        <li><strong>Source needed:</strong> directionally useful, but not public fact yet.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}research/`}>Read the research files →</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Charlie Buster / Grime Art</h2>
      <p>The raw visual layer behind NO BALL GAMES.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Visual language</span>
        <h3>Graffiti texture + grime energy</h3>
        <p>
          Grime Art is used here as the gritty UK visual layer: spray marks, stencil attitude, portrait punch, estate textures, painted clothing and one-of-one pieces with premium finish but raw edge.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Brand relationship</span>
        <h3>Separate, connected roles</h3>
        <p>
          Grime Art is the visual language. NO BALL GAMES is one of the worlds it can build. This keeps artist voice and brand universe aligned without collapsing them into one claim.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Claim caution</span>
        <h3>Source-safe public wording</h3>
        <p>
          Early-role history, collaboration details, celebrity mentions and named brand case studies should be published as verified facts only when public sources or project-owned proof are attached.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Growth timeline</h2>
      <p>How the system expands without overclaiming.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Origin</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Street sign as symbol</h3>
          <p>The phrase is lifted from real-world restriction signage and reframed as cultural identity.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Visual layer</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Grime Art enters the brand</h3>
          <p>Charlie Buster's visual direction feeds walls, clothing, portrait energy and the raw texture of the public pages.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Universe</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Lore and collector expansion</h3>
          <p>The world extends into collections, project lanes, XRP KIDs canon and community participation while separating lore from verified chain fact.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Go deeper</span>
      <h2>Use the archive before making hard claims.</h2>
      <p>The truth files hold the canon baseline, source-needed notes and rights policy that shape the public pages.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}research/`}>Open research vault</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}projects/`}>View projects</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
